ption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2007-469f2"/></fig><fig id="f3-bmi-2007-469" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Structural equation modeling for mediation effect. Dependent variable Ki-67 is predicted with single-headed EGFR and p-AKT. Each single-headed arrow represents a regression weights. Age and gender are considered to be associated with all the three biomarkers and are also allowed to be correlated and represented with double-headed arrow. Circles of e1, e2 and d1 are error terms with mean at 0 and variance at 1.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2007-469f3"/></fig><fig id="f4-bmi-2007-469" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Expression of EGFR and p-AKT. Left panel: membrane staining in tumor cells with EGFR; right panel: nuclear and cytoplasmic staining in tumor cells with p-AKT.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2007-469f4"/></fig><fig id="f5-bmi-2007-469" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Scatter plots with lowess lines. Circles are data points and lines are the lowess smoothing lines.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2007-469f5"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-bmi-2007-469" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Characteristic of the patients (N = 69).</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Characteristic</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Measurement</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Age (mean &#x000b1; SD)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28.9 &#x000b1; 15.6</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Female (%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">33 (48%)</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" align="left" rowspan="1">Diagnosis (%)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;osteoblastic</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">49 (71%)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;chondroblastic</td><td align="left" 